.TH RM 1
.SH NAME
rm \- remove files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rm
[
.B \-fr
]
.I file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Rm
removes files or directories.
A directory is removed only if it is empty.
The options are
.TP
.B \-f
Don't report files that can't be removed.
.TP
.B \-r
Recursively delete the
entire contents of a directory
and the directory itself.
.SH SOURCE
.B cmd/rm/main.odin
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR remove (2)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
The exit status is empty, or
.B "can't remove"
when a file could not be removed and
.B \-f
was not given.
The remaining files are still removed.
.SH BUGS
.B \-f
silences every failure, not only a missing file.
